// Default propagation models for native frontends (VirtualMethodTable::Native -- pcode today).
//
// Propagation only. CTADL ships no default sources or sinks: `cli::index` uses only the
// `summary` half of a loaded model batch, so the `sources`/`sinks` entries this file used to
// carry were parsed, validated, and discarded on every index. Their presence implied CTADL
// ships default endpoints, which it does not. Three generators here were endpoints and nothing
// else (`fgets`/`getenv`/... sources, `read`/`fread`/... sources, `system`/`exec*` sinks); they
// went with the entries.
//
// ACCESS PATHS. `.deref` is an ordinary symbol segment -- pcode's spelling for a pointee -- so
// it behaves as written. `.[<n>]` is a real `PathSegment::Offset` and matches what pcode emits;
// a field whose *name* begins with `[` would have to be escaped (`.\[...]`), which pcode never
// needs. A port pair is a PREFIX SUBSTITUTION, not a filter: `Argument(0).deref -> Return`
// unwraps a level, `Argument(0) -> Return.deref` adds one. See docs/model-generators.md §7 and
// the fixtures in `tests/tnt/port_*.tnt`.
//
// SYMBOL ALIASES. Firmware rarely imports the plain libc name: glibc/uClibc emit `_FORTIFY`
// wrappers (`__memcpy_chk`, `__strcpy_chk`, ...) and C99-conformance wrappers
// (`__isoc99_sscanf`), and Mach-O prefixes every C symbol with `_` -- so macOS produces
// `___strcpy_chk`, with three.
//
// They are listed here WITHOUT their leading underscores, because that is the name a model can
// actually match. The pcode frontend derives a function's VMT simple name with
// `func_data.name.trim_start_matches('_')` (`languages/pcode/mod.rs`), so `__memcpy_chk`,
// `___strcpy_chk` and `_strdup` reach the matcher as `memcpy_chk`, `strcpy_chk` and `strdup`.
// A `names` list spelling the underscores back on matches NOTHING -- not the simple name, which
// has been stripped, and not the fully-qualified one, which still carries Ghidra's
// `<EXTERNAL>::…@addr`. `nightly/tests/c/defaultmodels.c` is the regression guard: on a
// fortifying host (macOS/clang fortifies even at -O0) its `strcpy` arrives as `___strcpy_chk`,
// and the case passes only because `strcpy_chk` is in the list. On a host that does not
// fortify it arrives as plain `strcpy` and the case still passes -- so it covers the alias path
// where it can and never depends on it.
//
// Every `_chk` variant takes *extra* size/flag arguments, but every model covering them is
// positional at index 0/1 or uses `Argument(*)`, so no index arithmetic is needed -- extending
// the `names` list is the whole fix. Aliases with no home generator are deliberately absent:
// `printf_chk` and `isoc99_fscanf` would need `printf` and `fscanf` generators, and neither
// exists (both were endpoint-only, see above).
//
// COST. `compute_arg_arity` takes the max over *actual call sites*, so `Argument(*)` on a
// variadic fans out to the widest call in the program: one 12-argument `snprintf` anywhere makes
// every `snprintf` summary 12x12 program-wide. The printf and scanf families are the only
// variadic `Argument(*)` users here; keep it that way. The allocator generator also uses
// `Argument(*)`, but on a fixed 1-2 argument signature, so its fan-out is bounded.
//
// ---- copying ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["strcpy","wcscpy","strncpy","wcsncpy","stpcpy","wcpcpy","stpncpy","wcpncpy","strcat","wcscat","strncat","wcsncat","strcpy_chk","strncpy_chk","stpcpy_chk","stpncpy_chk","strcat_chk","strncat_chk","wcscpy_chk","wcsncpy_chk","wcscat_chk","wcsncat_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref"},{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["memcpy","memmove","mempcpy","memccpy","bcopy","memcpy_chk","memmove_chk","mempcpy_chk","memccpy_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref"},{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// `strlcpy(dst, src, siz)` / `strlcat(dst, src, siz)`: only `src` is a pointer. The BSD
// signature has no `Return` buffer either -- it returns the length it tried to create.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["strlcpy","strlcat","strlcpy_chk","strlcat_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref"}]}}
// ---- formatting and parsing ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["sprintf","swprintf","snprintf","vsprintf","vsnprintf","vswprintf","asprintf","vasprintf","sprintf_chk","snprintf_chk","vsprintf_chk","vsnprintf_chk","swprintf_chk","vswprintf_chk","asprintf_chk","vasprintf_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(*).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref"},{"input":"Argument(*).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["sscanf","swscanf","vsscanf","vswscanf","isoc99_sscanf","isoc99_swscanf","isoc99_vsscanf","isoc99_vswscanf"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Argument(*).deref"},{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// ---- duplication ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["strdup","strndup","wcsdup"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// ---- search: a pointer INTO the argument comes back ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["strchr","strrchr","wcschr","wcsrchr","strpbrk","wcspbrk","strstr","wcsstr","strtok","wcstok","strsep","strcasestr","index","rindex","memchr","memrchr","memmem","rawmemchr"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// `strtok_r(str, delim, saveptr)`: the state pointer keeps a pointer into `str`, so the taint
// has to survive to the next call. `Argument(2).deref.deref` is a two-level shift -- see
// `tests/tnt/port_two_segment.tnt`.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["strtok_r","wcstok_r"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"},{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Argument(2).deref.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["bsearch","lsearch","lfind"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// ---- length and numeric conversion: the RESULT is a scalar, so no `.deref` on the output ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["strlen","wcslen","strnlen","wcsnlen"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["atoi","atol","atoll","atof","strtol","strtoll","strtoul","strtoull","strtof","strtod","strtold","wcstol","wcstoll","wcstoul","wcstoull","wcstof","wcstod","wcstold"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["toupper","tolower","toascii"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0)","output":"Return"}]}}
// Byte-order swaps are pure scalar transforms. Firmware parsers are full of them, and dropping
// taint at one silently ends a flow that a length or offset field is driving.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["ntohl","ntohs","ntohll","htonl","htons","htonll","bswap_16","bswap_32","bswap_64"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0)","output":"Return"}]}}
// ---- line readers: a `char **` out-parameter, so the destination is two levels deep ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["getline"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(2).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["getdelim"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(3).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref.deref"}]}}
// ---- paths ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["basename","dirname"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["realpath","realpath_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Argument(1).deref"},{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["readlink","readlink_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Argument(1).deref"}]}}
// `readlinkat(dirfd, path, buf, bufsiz)` -- one argument to the right of `readlink`.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["readlinkat","readlinkat_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Argument(2).deref"}]}}
// ---- addresses ----
// `inet_ntoa(struct in_addr)` takes its argument BY VALUE, so the input port is bare.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["inet_ntoa"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0)","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["inet_ntop"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Argument(2).deref"},{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["inet_addr","inet_network","inet_aton"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return"},{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Argument(1).deref"}]}}
// `inet_pton(af, src, dst)` -- one argument to the right of `inet_aton`.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["inet_pton"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Argument(2).deref"},{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Return"}]}}
// ---- time ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["strftime","wcsftime","strftime_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(3).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref"}]}}
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["ctime","asctime","ctime_r","asctime_r"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// ---- wide / multibyte ----
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["mbstowcs","wcstombs","mbstowcs_chk","wcstombs_chk"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref","output":"Argument(0).deref"}]}}
// `mbsrtowcs(dest, &src, len, ps)` -- `src` is a `char **`, one level deeper than `mbstowcs`.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["mbsrtowcs","wcsrtombs"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(1).deref.deref","output":"Argument(0).deref"}]}}
// ---- allocation ----
// `Argument(*) -> Return.deref` is not a claim that the size taints the buffer. It exists to
// MATERIALIZE `Return.deref` as a vertex, so that a later write through the returned pointer has
// somewhere to land. Reads as a bug otherwise -- it is not one. `realloc` is separate below
// because for it the shape *is* wrong.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["malloc","calloc","aligned_alloc","valloc","memalign","posix_memalign"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(*)","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// `realloc(ptr, size)` KEEPS the old contents. Modeling it like `malloc` drops them, which ends
// a flow through every grow-the-buffer loop in a parser.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["realloc","reallocarray","reallocf"]}],"model":{"propagation":[{"input":"Argument(0).deref","output":"Return.deref"}]}}
// ---- the C++ exception unwinder ----
// These carry NO propagation and exist purely for `modes: ["skip-analysis"]`, which tells the
// indexer to derive nothing from their bodies. That is the whole model: an unwinder moves
// register and stack state to resume at a landing pad, not application data between a caller's
// arguments, so "this function propagates nothing" is the accurate summary rather than a
// convenient one. Taint arriving in a thrown object and leaving at a `catch` never crossed these
// frames as a data-flow edge anyway -- the personality routine writes it into a register the
// handler reads, which no access path in the IR names.
//
// The cost of NOT modeling them is not a missed flow, it is the analysis not finishing. On
// `remote_control_smack` (TaintBench, ARM native libraries) the three `__aeabi_unwind_cpp_pr*`
// personality routines summarize to ~50,000 rows EACH -- against a median of 1 row per function
// -- because an unwinder makes nearly everything reachable from nearly everything. They are also
// legitimate indirect-call targets, reached through a pointer in the exception table, so hybrid
// inlining instantiates those summaries at their call sites and the result multiplies through
// `context_assign` / `context_locals`. `tests/tnt/skip_analysis_hybrid.tnt` is that shape in
// miniature.
//
// `skip-analysis` and not a `propagation` list: a model ADDS to what a body derives. Only this
// directive replaces it. And the seed is the point -- suppressing just the summary rows would
// leave the body's `critical_summary` resolvents, which are what multiply.
//
// NAMES have their leading underscores stripped, per the SYMBOL ALIASES note at the top of this
// file: `__aeabi_unwind_cpp_pr0` reaches the matcher as `aeabi_unwind_cpp_pr0` and
// `_Unwind_RaiseException` as `Unwind_RaiseException`. Capital `U` in the `_Unwind_*` family is
// deliberate -- `signature_match` is exact, not case-folded.
{"find":"methods","where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","names":["aeabi_unwind_cpp_pr0","aeabi_unwind_cpp_pr1","aeabi_unwind_cpp_pr2","gnu_unwind_frame","gnu_unwind_execute","gnu_unwind_pr_common","gnu_Unwind_Resume","gnu_Unwind_Resume_or_Rethrow","gnu_Unwind_RaiseException","gnu_Unwind_ForcedUnwind","gnu_Unwind_Backtrace","unwind_phase1","unwind_phase2","unwind_phase2_forced","Unwind_RaiseException","Unwind_Resume","Unwind_Resume_or_Rethrow","Unwind_ForcedUnwind","Unwind_DeleteException","Unwind_Backtrace","Unwind_Complete","Unwind_VRS_Get","Unwind_VRS_Set","Unwind_VRS_Pop","Unwind_GetLanguageSpecificData","Unwind_GetRegionStart","Unwind_GetDataRelBase","Unwind_GetTextRelBase","cxa_begin_cleanup","cxa_end_cleanup","cxa_type_match","cxa_call_unexpected"]}],"model":{"modes":["skip-analysis"]}}
// ---- deliberately absent ----
// `qsort`/`heapsort`/`mergesort` used to carry `Argument(0).deref -> Argument(0).deref`, a
// self-loop that derives nothing: the taint it would propagate is already at the vertex it
// propagates to. Dropped rather than kept as documentation.
